<!--
  Static rather than generated: this site has a handful of public pages and a
  build step that emits a sitemap is a build step that can silently stop
  emitting one. Add a URL here when a public page is added.
-->
<urlset xmlns="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9">
  <url>
    <loc>https://sal0mander.com/</loc>
    <changefreq>weekly</changefreq>
    <priority>1.0</priority>
  </url>
  <!--
    The three activity links.

    These are the URLs a teacher actually shares — pasted into Classroom or
    printed as a QR code — so they matter more than any other page here. They
    are listed for two reasons.

    First, status. GitHub Pages cannot rewrite URLs, so a client-side route is
    served the SPA shell with an HTTP 404. `prerender-routes.mjs` derives its
    file list FROM this sitemap, so listing a URL here is what makes it resolve
    200. Unlisted, a shared activity link renders fine for a student and reads
    as missing to every crawler and filter classifier that checks it.

    Second, content. A domain categorised "Unknown" is one nobody has looked
    at. Three named activity pages are a stronger Education signal than four
    pages of policy text.

    Listed by hand because this file is deliberately static, and kept honest by
    a test: `discoverability.test.ts` asserts one entry here per activity in
    `MOCK_DEMO_ACTIVITIES`, so adding an activity without adding its URL fails
    the build rather than shipping a 404.
  -->
  <url>
    <loc>https://sal0mander.com/play/act_integer_operations</loc>
    <changefreq>monthly</changefreq>
    <priority>0.9</priority>
  </url>
  <url>
